From 667e79a2c1801bfd120f7b16ab706b921313fe26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/32] iOS: Options dialog for small touch screens

On iOS the Options dialog works like the Settings app: a category list,
pages with a back button, and pages fitted to the phone width. The layout
code itself lives in the iOS app layer (app/ios/options_ios.cpp in the
opencpn-ios repository); options.cpp gets the hooks that call it and the
iOS layout of single controls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gui/include/gui/options.h       |  32 +++
 gui/src/options.cpp             | 358 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 model/include/model/ios_hooks.h |   9 +-
 3 files changed, 393 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

